---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections & Clarifications Policy"
  description="CryptoPulse procedure for acknowledging, correcting, and documenting factual errors promptly and transparently."
  canonicalUrl="https://cryptopulse.news/corrections"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-slate-800">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-3">
        Corrections & Factual Accountability Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Committed to immediate, transparent, and public accountability.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <section class="bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-xl">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-3">Our Transparent Correction Protocol</h2>
        <p>When a factual error is discovered or brought to our attention by readers, subjects of reporting, or internal review, our newsroom takes prompt action:</p>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 mt-3 space-y-2 text-slate-400">
          <li><strong>Immediate Investigation:</strong> The senior editor on duty verifies the claim against primary source material and blockchain explorers.</li>
          <li><strong>Correction Note:</strong> If an error occurred, the article text is corrected immediately, and an explicit <em>Correction Notice</em> is appended to the top or bottom of the article specifying what was amended, the date and time, and the original wording.</li>
          <li><strong>No "Stealth Editing":</strong> We strictly prohibit quiet modifications of substantive factual errors without an accompanying explanatory notice.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-slate-900/50 border border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-xl">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-3">How to Request a Correction</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">To report a factual inaccuracy, please email our standards editor directly with the following:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-400">
          <li>The URL of the article in question.</li>
          <li>The specific paragraph or data point deemed inaccurate.</li>
          <li>Primary verifiable reference documents or on-chain transaction hash links proving the claim.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-4 p-3 bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 rounded-lg text-xs font-mono text-amber-400">
          corrections@cryptopulse.news
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>